{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931768-magic-item-creation-rules","id":931768,"title":"Magic item creation rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-14T19:51:51-07:00","id":931768,"title":"Magic item creation rules?","content":"Has anyone tried making &quot;blue book&quot; rules for creating magic items, like the kinds we've seen in Reliquary/the AKD/this forum's magic item thread? I admit it would probably be kind of hard to work out, since magic items can have such widely varied effects. <br /> <br /> I think we could try pulling some stuff from Genius' wonder creation rules, especially in terms of rolling for or choosing flaws. I'd like it to be a part of the rules that every magic item has to have some sort of flaw or cost- this is a horror game, after all. While you could set up a random roll table, I think the player and the GM should both be able to suggest flaws as an alternative, because that's a chance to get really creative. With effects, there are two ways to go. The player could describe the specific effect and work with the GM on the skills/resources/rolls required to make it, but I also like the idea of the player or the character going into it with only a vague outline and not being sure what they'll end up with. So the player decides that his character wants a charm that will protect him from possession, so the player and the GM work out a power and a flaw, and roleplay the character gathering the materials. Or, alternately, the player leaves it up to either the GM or a dice roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T19:55:03-07:00","id":931773,"title":"","content":"Reliquary has a system for creating magical items, basically like Hunter Endowments.<br /> <br /> Hunter essentially has one as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T04:58:04-07:00","id":931929,"title":"","content":"Reliquary and the 2E Equipment rules are pretty much it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T05:25:07-07:00","id":931939,"title":"","content":"Item Creation from <b>CoD Rulebook</b> is not enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"